card.statement:
The left $\Sj$-action on $\Td$ via the convolution product

\[
\Sj \times \Td \longrightarrow \Td
\]

is given as follows: for $1\le i \le n$,

\begin{align}
\E_i e_{r_1\cdots r_d} = v^{-# \{1 \leq k \leq D\vert r_k=i+1\}}
\sum_{\substack{\{1 \leq p \leq D \vert r_p=i\}}} v^{2#\{1 \leq j <p \vert r_j=i+1\}} e_{r'_1\cdots r'_d},
\end{align}

where
$\mbf r' = (r_1', \dots, r_D')$ for each $p$ with $r_p =i$ satisfies $r_s'=r_s$ (for $s\neq p, D+1-p$), $r'_p =i+1$, and $r'_{D+1-p} =N-i$;

\begin{align}
\F_i e_{r_1\cdots r_d} = v^{-#\{ 1 \leq k \leq D\vert r_k=i\}} \sum_{\substack{\{1 \leq p \leq D \vert r_p=i+1\}}} v^{2#\{p< j \leq D\mid r_j=i\}} e_{r''_1\cdots r''_d},
\end{align}

where $\mbf r'' = (r_1'', \dots, r_D'')$ for each $r_p =i+1$ satisfies $r''_s=r_s$ (for $s\neq p$, $D+1-p$), $r''_p=i$, and $r''_{D+1-p} =N+1-i$;
and
$
\mbf d_a^{\pm} e_{r_1\cdots r_d}
=v^{\mp #\{1\le  j\le D | r_j=a\} }
e_{r_1\cdots r_d}.
$
